      "id": 1,
      "text": "Friday Harbor became the county seat of San Juan County in 1873, the same year the Pig War ended peacefully.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://fridayharbor.org/2231/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Hudson's Bay Company sheepherder Joe Friday, who once worked the islands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://fridayharbor.org/2231/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A National Park Service historic walk at American Camp lets visitors stroll the trails of the Pig War era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fridayharbor.com/historic"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Each May, Friday Harbor celebrates National Historic Preservation Month with guided tours, talks, and special events at the historical museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fridayharbor.com/historic"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Friday Harbor lies in a rain shadow created by the Vancouver Island Ranges and the Olympic Mountains, making it drier than nearby areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
